                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Alone in the Dark 2 takes the wonderfully strange foundation of the original and somehow makes it even stranger. The increased emphasis on action and its bizarre mixture of horror, gangsters, pirates, and supernatural nonsense give it a personality entirely its own. There are some really neat ideas here, and for its time it remained an ambitious and impressive game. Unfortunately, increased action also means spending even more time fighting with controls and combat that have aged about as gracefully as milk. Playing it on a modern PC can be enormously frustrating, but underneath all that jank is still a creative and entertaining piece of early survival horror history.",
